# The Finale — not a board, a payoff (CANON 3.4).
# The victory lap: every character you helped says yes in the shape of their
# own arc. Nobody done it. Everybody fixes it.

@node f_iris_talk
  IRIS(worried): Please do not tell anyone how long I have been up here.
  YOU:
    * (kind) Seven days. And nobody is going to laugh.  -> f_iris_kind
    * (curious) You have been here the whole time.  -> f_iris_whole
    * (dry) I have been paid quite a lot of a small town's savings to tell people exactly that.  -> f_iris_dry

@node f_iris_kind
  IRIS(moved): ...You counted the sill.
  IRIS: I have been rehearsing being found for six days and I had it much
  better than this.
  goto f_iris_why

@node f_iris_whole
  IRIS(sad): The whole time. The stair went as I came off it. I have shouted
  a great deal into a great deal of harbour wind.
  goto f_iris_why

@node f_iris_dry
  IRIS(laughing): Oh, that is fair. That is entirely fair.
  goto f_iris_why

@node f_iris_why
  IRIS(sad): It has been cracking for three years. I could see it. I am the
  only one close enough to see it and I did not tell a soul.
  YOU:
    * (kind) Why not?  -> f_iris_pride
    * (curious) You ordered braces from your aunt and paid for them yourself.  -> f_iris_braces
    * (dry) You borrowed a locksmith's picks to burgle your own tower.  -> f_iris_braces

@node f_iris_braces
  IRIS: Four of them. Brass, lined. I have been mending it a piece at a time
  for a year, at night, so nobody would have to worry.
  goto f_iris_pride

@node f_iris_pride
  IRIS(sad): Because it is my job. Because my mother did it and hers did, and
  because —
  IRIS(moved): Because nobody else noticed. Three years and nobody else
  noticed, and I could not decide whether that made me the only one who cared
  or the only one who was left.
  YOU:
    * (kind) They noticed. They just did not know what they were looking at.  -> f_iris_noticed
    * (curious) So you came up alone at midnight with a borrowed set of picks.  -> f_iris_alone
    * (dry) You could simply have said something at the bakery.  -> f_iris_alone

@node f_iris_alone
  IRIS(sad): Yes. And the stair went behind me, and Pip has been shouting at
  the entire town for a week on my behalf, and they decided he was a thief.
  goto f_iris_noticed

@node f_iris_noticed
  IRIS(worried): It does not matter now. It cannot be lit, detective. Not by
  me and not by you. A cracked Prism cannot be re-lit by one person with a
  match. It has never worked like that.
  YOU:
    * (kind) I know exactly how it works. So do you.  -> f_iris_how
    * (curious) Then how does it work?  -> f_iris_how
    * (dry) Fortunately I have spent four days meeting absolutely everyone.  -> f_iris_how

@node f_iris_how
  IRIS(sad): It drinks a gathering. The whole town on the green with a light
  each. That is the mechanism. That is the only mechanism.
  IRIS(sad): They have not come in three years. They will not come tonight
  because a detective asked them to.
  YOU:
    * (kind) They will come because I am going to ask each of them by name.  -> f_iris_yes
    * (dry) Watch me.  -> f_iris_yes
    * (curious) Do you want to bet on that?  -> f_iris_yes

@node f_iris_yes
  set f.iris_told = 1
  IRIS(moved): ...There is a bell rope by the window. Nona's bell. It has not
  been rung since before I had this job.
  IRIS: If you are going to be absurd about this, be properly absurd.

@node f_iris_ask
  [if flag f.iris_told == 1]
  IRIS(happy): Go on then. Ring it.
  [else]
  goto f_iris_talk
  [end]

@node f_rally
  You pull the rope, and Nona's bell goes over Prismbrook for the first time
  in three years, and the town comes out into the street to find out who has
  died.
  Then you go down and you ask them. One at a time. By name.
  BRUNO(happy): Lantern-buns. Two hundred. Do not argue with me, I have
  already started the dough.
  TANSY(laughing): I will do the invitations! I will do ALL the invitations!
  OTTO(shifty): I will bring a pail. For the bird. It is a festival, he
  should have a festival too.
  GRETA(moved): The bunting has been up for three years, dear. It has been
  waiting longer than anybody.
  FELIX: Every house by six. I have walked worse rounds for worse reasons.
  MARIBEL: I will hold the last ferry. I have never held the last ferry.
  EDWINA(moved): I shall bring the braces. And I shall stand where she can
  see me.
  BARTLEBY(happy): I shall bring the ledger and begin a new page, which is the
  single most exciting sentence I have ever said.
  PETRA: I kept my promise. Now I would like to keep hers.
  SAGE(happy): The beds can wait a night. The beds have waited three years.
  MO(moved): The bees will not come. But they have known the way the whole
  time and I would like it noted.
  POPPY(laughing): I shall bring tea, and I shall stand near the Mayor in
  case he faints, which he will.
  MAYOR(worried): Eleven people came. The last time. Eleven.
  YOU:
    * (kind) Then this time you will have counted wrong.  -> f_mayor_yes
    * (dry) Bring a bigger tin of matches, Mayor.  -> f_mayor_yes
    * (curious) How many live in Prismbrook, Mayor?  -> f_mayor_yes

@node f_mayor_yes
  MAYOR(moved): ...Four hundred and six.
  MAYOR(happy): Four hundred and six. Right. Right! I shall need my other
  hat.
  NONA(moved): I will light the first wick.
  NONA: I have had it in my apron pocket for three years, since you ask. The
  match. Not the key. The match.
  play_cut f_festival
  end
